{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Santana IV feels like a natural follow-up to Hendrix and Clapton because expressive guitar playing is what draws me in right now; it was the one choice compelling enough for me to act on.",
    "The Rolling Stones and the Doors connect with the blues-rooted rock I have recently chosen, while the Beatles and Kinks reflect some of the songwriting appeal in my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Carpenters Gold and Glen Campbell's hits do not offer the blues and guitar-driven sound I am seeking, even though they sit alongside other familiar older music.",
    "Hejira's reflective, jazz-influenced direction and folklore do not feel like close follow-ups to my recent choices, while several otherwise appealing rock selections are compilations I would pass over today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat familiar older artists as broadly interchangeable, when the particular sound matters more to me than their era.",
    "There is too much emphasis on greatest-hits collections; recognizing an artist or liking their style does not give me enough reason to choose a retrospective today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my Hendrix and Clapton choices is expressive, blues-rooted guitar playing, which makes Santana IV especially appealing.",
    "My recent choices suggest interest in individual albums, and today a promising album feels more inviting than another collection of familiar hits."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You picked up on my interest in classic rock, but stretched it too broadly across older music and compilations instead of focusing on the guitar-driven albums most likely to draw me in."
}
